# Data-Driven Configuration

Character OS content is configuration, not code.

## Layout

- `characters/<id>/character.yaml` — character identity, personality, goals
- `characters/<id>/assets/` — portraits, audio refs, optional prompt overrides
- `worlds/<id>/world.yaml` — shared world metadata and knowledge index
- `worlds/<id>/knowledge/` — reusable lore (YAML entries)
- `prompts/*.md` — LLM templates loaded at runtime

## Rules

- New characters = new folder + YAML. No application code changes.
- World knowledge is shared via world packs; characters only add private `knowledge` entries.
- Prompts are Markdown templates with `{{variables}}`. Business logic stays in Python.
- Reference `docs/CONFIGURATION.md` for schemas and the loading contract.
